Abstract = {{We propose a novel central clearing counterparty (CCP) design for a
   financial network, in which the participation of banks in the CCP
   depends on the proportional clearing fee. We obtain the optimal fee that
   maximizes the CCP's net worth. We show that partial participation of
   banks in the CCP at the optimal fee rate reduces banks' aggregate
   shortfall and also reduces the overall systemic risk. We also carry out
   numerical examples to verify the theoretical results. (C) 2018 Elsevier
   B.V. All rights reserved.}},
